# Power moves to the other guide in lambda / (2 (n_even - n_odd)) = 49.47 um, from the supermodes of the transverse grid.
# Reference: full transfer at that length, half at half of it. Monitors use the modes of the separate guides, which overlap slightly at small gaps.
title Directional coupler, two 0.5 um guides 300 nm apart
window width=14 length=101
guide straight x=-0.4 width=0.5 from=0 to=101
guide straight x=0.4 width=0.5 from=0 to=101
launch mode x=-0.4 width=0.5
monitor half_cross z=24.75 x=0.4 width=0.5
monitor cross_full z=49.5 x=0.4 width=0.5
monitor bar_full z=49.5 x=-0.4 width=0.5
monitor bar_end z=101 x=-0.4 width=0.5
monitor cross_end z=101 x=0.4 width=0.5
expect power half_cross 0.500787658 2e-7
expect power cross_full 0.999951233 2e-7
expect power bar_full 0.000628536 2e-7
expect power bar_end 0.995256589 2e-7
expect power cross_end 0.004892626 2e-7
expect neff 2.636740334 2e-8
expect power_above cross_full 0.995
expect power_below bar_full 0.005
expect power half_cross 0.5 0.02
expect sum bar_end cross_end 1.0 0.002
